GAL22V10
VJVHDECR5

DOTCLK HC0 HC1 HC2 HC3 HC4 HC5 HC6 HC7 HC8 HC9 GND
RESETn HEND /HSYNCn HACTIVE BYTETICK /FILOADn /SRLOADn SRINH FETCH RBSTROBE NC VCC

; 640x480 timing: horizontal counter runs 0..799 and is asynchronously
; cleared when the decode reaches 800.  Reset also asserts the clear.
HEND = /RESETn
     + HC9 * HC8 * /HC7 * /HC6 * HC5 * /HC4 * /HC3 * /HC2 * /HC1 * /HC0

; Negative sync is low for counts 656..751 inclusive.
/HSYNCn = RESETn * HC9 * /HC8 * HC7 * /HC6 * /HC5 * HC4
         + RESETn * HC9 * /HC8 * HC7 * /HC6 * HC5
         + RESETn * HC9 * /HC8 * HC7 * HC6 * /HC5
         + RESETn * HC9 * /HC8 * HC7 * HC6 * HC5 * /HC4

; Visible dots 0..639.
HACTIVE = RESETn * /HC9
        + RESETn * /HC8 * /HC7

; A byte occupies 16 dots.  SRAM owns phases 12..15; phase 0 loads the
; shifter and advances the scan index only while the visible line is active.
FETCH = RESETn * HC3 * HC2
/SRLOADn = RESETn * /HC3 * /HC2 * /HC1 * /HC0
SRINH = RESETn * HC0
BYTETICK = RESETn * /HC3 * /HC2 * /HC1 * /HC0 * /HC9
         + RESETn * /HC3 * /HC2 * /HC1 * /HC0 * /HC8 * /HC7

; Reload the scan index from ROW_BASE at dot 784.  The final fetch at
; dots 796..799 then prefetches byte zero before the next visible line.
/FILOADn = RESETn * HC9 * HC8 * /HC7 * /HC6 * /HC5 * HC4
         * /HC3 * /HC2 * /HC1 * /HC0

; At dot 640, capture base+40 on odd VGA lines.  U6 gates this pulse with VC0.
RBSTROBE = RESETn * HC9 * /HC8 * HC7 * /HC6 * /HC5 * /HC4
         * /HC3 * /HC2 * /HC1 * /HC0

DESCRIPTION

VJUGA rev B Video-card U5 horizontal timing, fetch and scan phases.
